{# Placeholder legal copy. This page exists because the checkout consent controls
   link to it, and a consent whose document cannot be opened is not consent at all
   (`[26.9]`). The wording below is deliberately not legal text — jurisdiction and
   counsel differ, and every deployment is responsible for its own. #}
{% extends 'layouts/marketing.twig' %}
{% set page_title = 'Telehealth Consent' %}
{% set page_description = 'Telehealth Consent for ' ~ site.name ~ '.' %}
{% block content %}

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:px-10 sm:py-24">
  <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold text-heading sm:text-4xl">Telehealth Consent</h1>

  <p role="note" class="mt-8 rounded-sm border border-danger bg-background px-5 py-4 text-sm font-medium text-danger">
    This page is placeholder text and is not legal advice. This deployment must
    replace it with its own Telehealth Consent before taking real orders.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-4 text-base text-body">
    <p>
      This document would set out what the patient is consenting to when they receive care remotely. It is linked from the consent
      controls on the checkout page, so a buyer is asked to agree to it before
      an order can be placed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The consent wording itself lives in <code>config/consent.php</code>, and the
      exact text shown to each buyer is stored with their order — so a record can
      always reproduce what was agreed to, rather than pointing at whatever this
      page happens to say later.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
